@majorheading Parallel computing in SINGULAR

The available ressources are given by the number of cpus
(set by the command line parameter @code{--cpus=..},
or the environment variable @code{SINGULAR_CPUS}, defaults to the
number of processors currently online) and the number of threads
(set by the command line parameter @code{--threads=..}, defaults to 1).
Threads are currently used with FLINT and NTL.@*
If @sc{Singular} is uses as a libary, the default are 1 in botrh cases.@*
Setting @code{--cpus} to 0 disables the creation of new processes and
chooses a sequentiell algorithm if possible.@*
Setting @code{--cpus} to 1 chooses a sequentiell algorithm in many cases.@*
Using parallel algorithms can reduce the overall computing time,
by can also increase the memory usage by a factor given by the
number of used cpu cores.

Via modular methods, requires QQ as coefficient field:
@itemize
@item assPrimes: @ref{assPrimes}
@item chinrem: @ref{chinrem}
@item farey: @ref{farey}
